# PNG plain   · insert BEFORE the line `                    <h3>Understanding Metal Colors</h3>`
                    <figure>
                        <img src="images/lesson_11_17_metallic_property_table.png"
                         alt="A comparison table of visual properties for non-metals (Metallic 0) versus metals (Metallic 1). Rows compare base color role, diffuse reflection, specular reflection, Fresnel range, color in shadows, and reflection color. Non-metals show a diffuse base color, weak colorless specular, a dramatic 4 to 100 percent Fresnel range, and white reflections. Metals show no diffuse, strong colored specular, a subtle 70 to 100 percent Fresnel range, dark shadows, and reflections tinted by the base color."
                         loading="lazy">
                        <figcaption>Side by side, the visual rules for non-metals and metals. The single biggest difference: metals have no diffuse component, so in shadow they go dark and only their reflections carry the look.</figcaption>
                    </figure>
